          "en": "(1) The settlement of a dispute of interests, a dispute over termination of employment or a dispute between trade unions only within one company through conciliation is carried out by a conciliator whose working area covers the place where the worker works.\n(2) The settlement …\n(2) The settlement by the conciliator as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out after the parties submit a written request for settlement to a conciliator appointed and agreed upon by the parties.\n(3) The parties may ascertain the name of the conciliator to be chosen and agreed upon from the list of conciliators posted and announced at the office of the local Government agency responsible for labour affairs.\n\nSufficiently clear\n\nSufficiently clear"
